WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.125
Long-lived AI systems do not merely retrieve context.

2
00:00:04.125 --> 00:00:09.715
They mutate durable memory through stores, branches, indexes, caches, summaries, replicas,

3
00:00:09.715 --> 00:00:11.240
and recovery paths.

4
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.347
A clean-looking prompt can still come from a mixed snapshot,

5
00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:18.737
an uncommitted write, a stale index, a foreign branch,

6
00:00:18.737 --> 00:00:22.880
or a derivative whose source was revoked. This chapter treats context

7
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:24.010
as accountable state.

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:29.892
A Context Transaction binds the principal, purpose, operation, base snapshot, branch,

9
00:00:29.892 --> 00:00:35.434
mounts, authority, rights, isolation, durability, budget, and support ceiling to the

10
00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:39.969
actual pre-state and every attempted, applied, visible, replayed, recovered,

11
00:00:39.969 --> 00:00:41.480
or indeterminate post-state.

12
00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:47.197
The transaction begins with an observed snapshot, not a friendly name

13
00:00:47.197 --> 00:00:52.313
or timestamp. It binds exact object versions, content and index epochs,

14
00:00:52.313 --> 00:00:56.965
causal parents, branch, mount policy, provenance, taint, leases, caches, backups,

15
00:00:56.965 --> 00:00:58.360
and open obligations.

16
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:03.610
The request declares intended reads, writes, derivations, deletions, and revocations,

17
00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:09.011
but the receipt records what actually happened. Purpose-bound mounts distinguish read,

18
00:01:09.011 --> 00:01:13.430
write, derive, delete, share, export, train, and execute permission.

19
00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:18.266
No cache, summary, branch, replica, or restore route may widen that

20
00:01:18.266 --> 00:01:18.675
envelope.

21
00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:25.155
Commit is a lifecycle, not a success boolean. Requested, admitted, prepared,

22
00:01:25.155 --> 00:01:29.432
applied, durably committed, consumer-visible, replayed, recovered, compensated, aborted,

23
00:01:29.432 --> 00:01:32.105
and indeterminate are different states.

24
00:01:32.445 --> 00:01:37.627
Content, indexes, provenance, taint, rights, derivative edges, deletion obligations, caches,

25
00:01:37.627 --> 00:01:43.327
and audit references commit atomically only inside the declared boundary. Conflicts,

26
00:01:43.327 --> 00:01:48.509
lost updates, write skew, stale indexes, retry duplicates, partial writes,

27
00:01:48.509 --> 00:01:51.100
and uncertain participants remain explicit.

28
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.548
Crash recovery must return to the declared durable frontier and compare

29
00:01:56.548 --> 00:01:58.870
independently observed state after restart.

30
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:04.014
Consider a source correction on branch B. A transaction reads snapshot

31
00:02:04.014 --> 00:02:07.731
forty-one through a purpose-bound mount, writes a corrected object,

32
00:02:07.731 --> 00:02:12.275
derives a summary and embedding, and invalidates an exact response cache.

33
00:02:12.615 --> 00:02:16.234
A concurrent branch changes the same semantic object,

34
00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:21.210
so silent last-writer-wins is forbidden. The transaction rebases or preserves both

35
00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:25.733
branches. Taint from the corrected source follows the summary, embedding,

36
00:02:25.733 --> 00:02:27.995
cache key, and downstream route.

37
00:02:28.335 --> 00:02:33.510
If deletion is later requested, closure walks live objects, indexes, caches,

38
00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:38.685
replicas, exports, and backups. An unreachable backup remains an owned residual;

39
00:02:38.685 --> 00:02:43.390
it cannot be relabeled as physical erasure or model forgetting.

40
00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:49.229
Caching makes the distinction especially important. Prefix caching reuses compatible model

41
00:02:49.229 --> 00:02:54.468
state and still produces a new answer. Response caching returns a

42
00:02:54.468 --> 00:02:55.420
prior answer.

43
00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.505
An exact response key therefore closes over request, consumer, model, decoding,

44
00:03:01.505 --> 00:03:07.251
tools, sources, schema, locale, time, authority, purpose, policy, rights, side-effect state,

45
00:03:07.251 --> 00:03:09.340
verifier, and dependency versions.

46
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:15.741
A semantic cache weakens the match further: similarity is only an

47
00:03:15.741 --> 00:03:21.801
approximate route candidate. Dynamic facts, personalized decisions, high-impact advice, security actions,

48
00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:26.760
rights-sensitive material, and side-effecting operations normally require fresh evaluation.

49
00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:31.780
Every hit discloses whether compatible prefill or a prior answer was

50
00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:32.205
reused.

51
00:03:32.805 --> 00:03:37.821
This design can still become transaction theater. A perfect log may

52
00:03:37.821 --> 00:03:42.837
describe bytes that never became durable. A database can protect records

53
00:03:42.837 --> 00:03:46.485
without preserving semantic identity, taint, or erasure categories.

54
00:03:46.825 --> 00:03:52.672
Deleting storage does not establish behavioral forgetting, influence removal, privacy protection,

55
00:03:52.672 --> 00:03:55.330
or removal from external descendants.

56
00:03:55.670 --> 00:04:00.946
The strongest current checks are finite: three valid and six invalid

57
00:04:00.946 --> 00:04:05.263
store fixtures, two valid and four invalid event sequences,

58
00:04:05.263 --> 00:04:09.100
seventy-eight rejected mutations, and one bounded historical-project lifecycle.

59
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:14.591
They establish record and route consequences, not concurrency, serializability,

60
00:04:14.591 --> 00:04:19.170
crash-safe deployed storage, complete invalidation, or useful memory.

61
00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:25.130
The core remains Design rationale at argument support and blocked after

62
00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:30.490
a full attempt. Its maximum inference is a bounded finite partially

63
00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:35.363
observed world-model result only—no open-world truth, general memory transfer, deployment,

64
00:04:35.363 --> 00:04:36.825
or chapter-core promotion.

65
00:04:37.165 --> 00:04:41.493
A valid context transaction says which state transition occurred within its

66
00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:45.821
declared boundary. It does not say that the context is true,

67
00:04:45.821 --> 00:04:47.395
sufficient, safe, or useful.

68
00:04:47.735 --> 00:04:51.233
The next chapter, Verification Bandwidth and Context Adequacy,

69
00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:56.043
asks that separate question: whether the system has enough evidence, tools,

70
00:04:56.043 --> 00:05:00.853
comparisons, contradiction search, and reviewer capacity to justify the claim it

71
00:05:00.853 --> 00:05:02.165
wants to make.
